Rym: GeekNights is distributed under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License.

691
00:52:50,830 --> 00:52:55,110
Scott: GeekNights is recorded live with no studio and no audience.

692
00:52:55,630 --> 00:52:59,090
Scott: But unlike those other late shows, it's actually recorded at night.

693
00:52:59,330 --> 00:53:12,809
Rym: And the Patreon and Patrons for this episode of GeekNights are Alan Joyce, Link E. G, Dredd, Lily Tenebrae, Kace, Kare, Maix, Musa, Chris, Adad, Christopher, Orr, Clinton, Walton, Finn, Joel Hayes, Benny Reimer, Rebecca Dunn, Sam Erickson, Trevor Van Horl, and a bunch of people who don't want me to say their names.

694
00:53:13,851 --> 00:53:14,715
Rym: Happy Holidays.

695
00:53:14,715 --> 00:53:17,106
Rym: 50/50 shot if we do a show tomorrow.

696
00:53:17,126 --> 00:53:18,070
Rym: Tonight.

697
00:53:19,150 --> 00:53:24,510
Rym: Senator Reverdy Johnson worried that the final version of Section 3 did not include the office of the presidency.

698
00:53:25,190 --> 00:53:33,588
Rym: He stated, "This amendment does not go far enough because past rebels may be elected president or vice president of the United

699
00:53:33,629 --> 00:53:33,909
Rym: States.".

700
00:53:34,370 --> 00:53:37,719
Rym: So, he asked, "Why did you omit to exclude them?

701
00:53:37,819 --> 00:53:43,094
Rym: I do not understand them to be excluded from the privilege of holding the two highest offices in the gift of the

702
00:53:43,134 --> 00:53:43,495
Rym: nation.".

703
00:53:44,640 --> 00:53:47,370
Rym: Senator Lott Morrill fielded this objection.

704
00:53:47,710 --> 00:53:56,128
Rym: He replied, "Let me call the Senator's attention to the words, 'or hold any office, civil or military, under the United

705
00:53:56,188 --> 00:53:56,529
Rym: States.'".

706
00:53:57,992 --> 00:54:04,765
Rym: This answer satisfied Senator Johnson, who stated, "Perhaps I am wrong as to the exclusion from the presidency.

707
00:54:05,466 --> 00:54:06,849
Rym: No doubt, I

708
00:54:07,009 --> 00:54:07,069
Rym: am.".

